<article class="env-corollary" id="55B0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/55B0">Corollary <span data-tag="55B0">6.2.3.11</span>.</a> Let $\calX $ be a semitopos, and let $\{  f_{\alpha }: X_{\alpha } \rightarrow Y_{\alpha } \} $ be a $($small$)$ collection of effective epimorphisms in $\calX $. Then the induced map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  f: \coprod _{\alpha } X_{\alpha } \rightarrow \coprod _{\alpha } Y_{\alpha }  \]
</div>
  <p> is an effective epimorphism. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Proposition <a href="/tag/9FB3" data-tag="9FB3">6.2.3.10</a> with Remark <a href="/tag/ED47" data-tag="ED47">6.2.3.9</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>